  "body": "### Root Cause  \nIn `transferFrom()`, the code does this:\n\n```solidity\nemit Transfer(msg.sender, to, amount);   // ← WRONG\n```\n\nBut the ERC-20 standard says the first argument must be the account whose tokens were taken (`from`), not the spender (`msg.sender`).\n\nCorrect version:\n```solidity\nemit Transfer(from, to, amount);         // ← CORRECT\n```\n\nBecause of this one-line mistake, every `transferFrom()` emits a lie in the event log.\n\n### Vulnerable Path  \n1. Alice calls `approve(Bob, 1000)`\n2. Bob calls `transferFrom(Alice → Bridge, 1000)`\n3. On-chain:  \n   - Alice’s balance −1000  \n   - Bridge balance +1000  \n   → everything correct\n4. Event emitted:\n   ```solidity\n   Transfer(Bob, Bridge, 1000)   // ← says Bob sent the tokens!\n   ```\n5. Any system that watches events thinks Bob owns and sent the tokens\n\n### Impact  \nBridges that credit based on Transfer events → mint tokens to Bob instead of Alice  \n\n\n\n### Recommendation\nToken violates the official standard(ERC-20 Non-Compliance). Change the Transfer event in `transferFrom()` to use `from` instead of `msg.sender`.",
  "proof_of_concept": "add this to `TokenWrapper.t.sol` and ran `forge test --match-contract TransferFromEventBugTest -vv`.\n```solidity\n\ncontract TokenWrapperPeripheryForBugTest is BaseLocker {\n    using FlashAccountantLib for *;\n\n    constructor(ICore _core) BaseLocker(_core) {}\n\n    function wrap(TokenWrapper wrapper, uint128 amount) external {\n        lock(abi.encode(wrapper, msg.sender, msg.sender, int256(uint256(amount))));\n    }\n\n    function wrap(TokenWrapper wrapper, address recipient, uint128 amount) external {\n        lock(abi.encode(wrapper, msg.sender, recipient, int256(uint256(amount))));\n    }\n\n    function handleLockData(uint256, bytes memory data) internal override returns (bytes memory) {\n        (TokenWrapper wrapper, address payer, address recipient, int256 amount) =\n            abi.decode(data, (TokenWrapper, address, address, int256));\n\n        if (amount >= 0) {\n            ACCOUNTANT.forward(address(wrapper), abi.encode(amount));\n            if (uint128(uint256(amount)) > 0) {\n                ACCOUNTANT.withdraw(address(wrapper), recipient, uint128(uint256(amount)));\n            }\n            if (uint256(amount) != 0) {\n                if (address(wrapper.UNDERLYING_TOKEN()) == NATIVE_TOKEN_ADDRESS) {\n                    SafeTransferLib.safeTransferETH(address(ACCOUNTANT), uint256(amount));\n                } else {\n                    ACCOUNTANT.payFrom(payer, address(wrapper.UNDERLYING_TOKEN()), uint256(amount));\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return \"\";\n    }\n}\n\ncontract TransferFromEventBugTest is FullTest {\n    TokenWrapperFactory factory;\n    TokenWrapperPeripheryForBugTest periphery;\n    TestToken underlying;\n    TokenWrapper wrapper;\n\n    address alice;\n    address spender;\n    address bridge;\n\n    // ERC-20 Transfer event signature\n    event Transfer(address indexed from, address indexed to, uint256 value);\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        FullTest.setUp();\n        \n        alice = makeAddr(\"alice\");\n        spender = makeAddr(\"spender\");\n        bridge = makeAddr(\"bridge\");\n        \n        underlying = new TestToken(address(this));\n        factory = new TokenWrapperFactory(core);\n        periphery = new TokenWrapperPeripheryForBugTest(core);\n        \n        // Deploy wrapper with unlock time in past so we can freely test\n        wrapper = factory.deployWrapper(IERC20(address(underlying)), block.timestamp - 1);\n        \n        // Mint underlying tokens to this contract and wrap them for Alice\n        underlying.approve(address(periphery), 1000 ether);\n        periphery.wrap(wrapper, alice, uint128(1000 ether));\n    }\n\n    /// @notice POC: Demonstrates transferFrom emits wrong 'from' address in Transfer event\n    /// @dev The bug: emit Transfer(msg.sender, to, amount) instead of emit Transfer(from, to, amount)\n    function test_POC_TransferFrom_Emits_Wrong_From_Address() public {\n        uint256 amount = 100 ether;\n\n        // Verify Alice has tokens\n        uint256 aliceBalance = wrapper.balanceOf(alice);\n        assertEq(aliceBalance, 1000 ether, \"Alice should have 1000 tokens\");\n\n        // Alice approves spender\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        wrapper.approve(spender, amount);\n\n        // Record balances before\n        uint256 aliceBalanceBefore = wrapper.balanceOf(alice);\n        uint256 bridgeBalanceBefore = wrapper.balanceOf(bridge);\n        uint256 spenderBalanceBefore = wrapper.balanceOf(spender);\n\n        // THE BUG: The event will emit Transfer(spender, bridge, amount)\n        // instead of the correct Transfer(alice, bridge, amount)\n        \n        // We expect the WRONG event (demonstrating the bug)\n        // Per ERC-20, it SHOULD be Transfer(alice, bridge, amount)\n        // But the buggy code emits Transfer(spender, bridge, amount)\n        vm.expectEmit(true, true, false, true, address(wrapper));\n        emit Transfer(spender, bridge, amount);  // BUG: Should be alice, not spender!\n\n        // Spender calls transferFrom\n        vm.prank(spender);\n        wrapper.transferFrom(alice, bridge, amount);\n\n        // Verify balances after - on-chain state is correct\n        uint256 aliceBalanceAfter = wrapper.balanceOf(alice);\n        uint256 bridgeBalanceAfter = wrapper.balanceOf(bridge);\n        uint256 spenderBalanceAfter = wrapper.balanceOf(spender);\n\n        // On-chain state is correct\n        assertEq(aliceBalanceAfter, aliceBalanceBefore - amount, \"Alice balance should decrease\");\n        assertEq(bridgeBalanceAfter, bridgeBalanceBefore + amount, \"Bridge balance should increase\");\n        assertEq(spenderBalanceAfter, spenderBalanceBefore, \"Spender balance should be unchanged\");\n    }\n\n    /// @notice Demonstrates that spender appears to transfer tokens they never owned\n    function test_POC_Spender_Never_Had_Tokens_But_Event_Says_They_Transferred() public {\n        uint256 amount = 500 ether;\n\n        // Verify spender has ZERO tokens before\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(spender), 0, \"Spender should have 0 tokens initially\");\n\n        // Alice approves spender\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        wrapper.approve(spender, amount);\n\n        // Expect the buggy event: spender appears as sender even though they have 0 tokens\n        vm.expectEmit(true, true, false, true, address(wrapper));\n        emit Transfer(spender, bridge, amount);  // BUG: Claims spender sent tokens\n\n        // Execute transferFrom\n        vm.prank(spender);\n        wrapper.transferFrom(alice, bridge, amount);\n\n        // Spender STILL has zero tokens - proving they never had any\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(spender), 0, \"Spender should still have 0 tokens\");\n        \n        // Alice lost the tokens\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(alice), 500 ether, \"Alice should have lost 500 tokens\");\n        \n        // Bridge received the tokens\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(bridge), amount, \"Bridge should have received tokens\");\n    }\n\n  \n    /// @notice Compare with standard transfer() which works correctly\n    function test_POC_Transfer_Correct_But_TransferFrom_Wrong() public {\n        uint256 amount = 100 ether;\n\n        // Test 1: transfer() emits correct event (alice -> bridge)\n        vm.expectEmit(true, true, false, true, address(wrapper));\n        emit Transfer(alice, bridge, amount);  // CORRECT: alice is the sender\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        wrapper.transfer(bridge, amount);\n\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(alice), 900 ether, \"Alice should have 900 tokens after transfer\");\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(bridge), 100 ether, \"Bridge should have 100 tokens\");\n\n        // Reset: bridge sends back to alice\n        vm.prank(bridge);\n        wrapper.transfer(alice, amount);\n\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(alice), 1000 ether, \"Alice should have 1000 tokens again\");\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(bridge), 0, \"Bridge should have 0 tokens\");\n\n        // Test 2: transferFrom() emits WRONG event (spender instead of alice)\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        wrapper.approve(spender, amount);\n\n        vm.expectEmit(true, true, false, true, address(wrapper));\n        emit Transfer(spender, bridge, amount);  // WRONG: should be alice\n\n        vm.prank(spender);\n        wrapper.transferFrom(alice, bridge, amount);\n\n        // Verify state is correct despite wrong event\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(alice), 900 ether, \"Alice should have 900 tokens\");\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(bridge), 100 ether, \"Bridge should have 100 tokens\");\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(spender), 0, \"Spender should have 0 tokens\");\n    }\n\n\n}\n```\nOutput:-\n\n```bash\nRan 3 tests for test/TokenWrapper.t.sol:TransferFromEventBugTest\n[PASS] test_POC_Spender_Never_Had_Tokens_But_Event_Says_They_Transferred() (gas: 62402)\n[PASS] test_POC_TransferFrom_Emits_Wrong_From_Address() (gas: 65615)\n[PASS] test_POC_Transfer_Correct_But_TransferFrom_Wrong() (gas: 92939)\nSuite result: ok. 3 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 19.52ms (9.32ms CPU time)\n\nRan 1 test suite in 70.40ms (19.52ms CPU time): 3 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (3 total tests)\n```",
